ubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134965659,imgsize-1050498.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Born with an underdeveloped arm, he built a LEGO prosthetic at 18 to help another boy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134966130.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/he-was-born-with-an-underdeveloped-arm-and-faced-hurtful-comments-as-a-child-at-18-he-built-a-working-lego-prosthetic-helping-an-8-year-old-boy-with-similar-limb-differences/articleshow/134966130.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/he-was-born-with-an-underdeveloped-arm-and-faced-hurtful-comments-as-a-child-at-18-he-built-a-working-lego-prosthetic-helping-an-8-year-old-boy-with-similar-limb-differences/articleshow/134966130.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T16:57:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134966312,imgsize-843642.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Who is Holden Bierman? American teen who built a sustainable swimwear brand with $500]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134965500.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At just 12 years old, Holden Bierman founded Coastal Cool during the pandemic with a modest $500 loan. Originally selling casual apparel, he shifted focus to creating eco-friendly swimwear made from recycled materials. By partnering with Tidey Ocean, Bierman supports ocean plastic removal with every sale. While managing his business, he sacrifices typical high school experiences but aims to expand retail and study business at university.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-holden-bierman-the-19-year-old-holly-springs-nc-entrepreneur-who-started-a-beachwear-brand-at-12-with-a-500-loan-six-years-later-it-is-a-six-figure-business-that-says-it-helped-remove-100000-plastic-bottles/articleshow/134965500.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-holden-bierman-the-19-year-old-holly-springs-nc-entrepreneur-who-started-a-beachwear-brand-at-12-with-a-500-loan-six-years-later-it-is-a-six-figure-business-that-says-it-helped-remove-100000-plastic-bottles/articleshow/134965500.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T16:30:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134965741,imgsize-1272251.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[What is causing the haze in Southeast Asia? Key facts explained]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134963891.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The ongoing wildfires in Indonesia have led to a sharp rise in respiratory issues across the region, significantly impacting air quality in neighboring countries like Singapore and Malaysia. This environmental crisis has caused escalating tensions as Indonesian officials feel mounting pressure to boost firefighting efforts and seek help from affected nations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/what-is-causing-the-haze-in-southeast-asia-key-facts-explained/articleshow/134963891.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/what-is-causing-the-haze-in-southeast-asia-key-facts-explained/articleshow/134963891.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T16:01:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134964836,imgsize-228381.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wyoming ranch visited by Queen Elizabeth II hits market for $24.5M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134964757.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Quarter Circle Lazy B Ranch, spanning 1,542 acres in Wyoming, is now on the market for $24.5 million. This family-owned property has been in the Wallop family since 1889 and hosted notable guests like Queen Elizabeth II. The ranch features a luxury lodge, multiple homes, and retains its panoramic mountain views and tranquility. Accessible to the town of Sheridan, the ranch offers both privacy and outdoor recreation opportunities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/founded-in-1889-by-an-english-earls-son-this-wyoming-ranch-stayed-in-the-family-for-four-generations-the-1542-acre-property-also-visited-by-queen-elizabeth-ii-hits-the-market-for-24-5-million/articleshow/134964757.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/founded-in-1889-by-an-english-earls-son-this-wyoming-ranch-stayed-in-the-family-for-four-generations-the-1542-acre-property-also-visited-by-queen-elizabeth-ii-hits-the-market-for-24-5-million/articleshow/134964757.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T16:16:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134964977,imgsize-360258.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tampa Theatre turns 100: Historic movie palace reopens after $24.5 million restoration]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134964170.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Tampa Theatre has successfully wrapped up an extensive restoration initiative that commenced earlier this year. This project focused on revamping treasured decorations and upgrading essential infrastructure for future enhancements. A newly added education wing will support community-driven programs and classes, bolstering its cultural significance. Historical artifacts have been recovered and restored, ensuring the protection of its legacy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1926-tampa-theatre-opened-beneath-a-twinkling-indoor-night-sky-100-years-later-it-reopened-after-a-seven-month-24-5-million-restoration-of-its-historic-auditorium/articleshow/134964170.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1926-tampa-theatre-opened-beneath-a-twinkling-indoor-night-sky-100-years-later-it-reopened-after-a-seven-month-24-5-million-restoration-of-its-historic-auditorium/articleshow/134964170.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T16:04:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134964280,imgsize-1389808.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hawaii’s Hā‘ena State Park reopens after 39 days following Hurricane Lowell]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134963256.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Hā‘ena State Park on Kaua‘i reopened on October 15 after being closed due to Hurricane Lowell. Visitors can now access specific hiking trails and Kē‘ē Beach, but restrictions remain. Overnight camping is still prohibited, while hiking beyond two miles along the Kalalau Trail is not allowed. Other state parks on Kaua‘i remain closed or have limited access due to extensive storm damage.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/hawaiis-hena-state-park-closed-sept-6-as-hurricane-lowell-approached-39-days-later-it-reopened-after-repairs-but-overnight-camping-and-hiking-past-two-miles-remain-closed/articleshow/134963256.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/hawaiis-hena-state-park-closed-sept-6-as-hurricane-lowell-approached-39-days-later-it-reopened-after-repairs-but-overnight-camping-and-hiking-past-two-miles-remain-closed/articleshow/134963256.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T16:03:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134963360,imgsize-1370028.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US bank worker stole $280,000 and used fake reports to hide it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134963596.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-bank-employee-stole-280000-from-a-vault-then-created-fake-cash-deposit-reports-to-hide-it-irs-helped-uncover-the-scheme/articleshow/134963596.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-bank-employee-stole-280000-from-a-vault-then-created-fake-cash-deposit-reports-to-hide-it-irs-helped-uncover-the-scheme/articleshow/134963596.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T15:21:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134963797,imgsize-120052.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oregon woman sold home to son-in-law, says he promised she could stay for life; court rejects claim]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134962876.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Oregon woman who sold her home worth approximately $398,000 to her son-in-law for $270,000 in 2006 claimed she was promised the right to live there for life. After a dispute over her occupancy, a trial court ruled in her favour. However, the Oregon Court of Appeals overturned the decision, finding that the written sale documents transferred her entire ownership interest without reserving a life estate.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2006-an-oregon-woman-sold-her-398000-home-to-her-son-in-law-for-270000-and-says-she-was-promised-she-could-stay-for-life-20-years-later-an-appeals-court-rejected-that-claimed-life-estate/articleshow/134962876.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2006-an-oregon-woman-sold-her-398000-home-to-her-son-in-law-for-270000-and-says-she-was-promised-she-could-stay-for-life-20-years-later-an-appeals-court-rejected-that-claimed-life-estate/articleshow/134962876.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T15:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134963376,imgsize-157698.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Amelia Earhart vanished in 1937; a theory suggests crabs consumed her remains as a castaway]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134964353.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/amelia-earhart-vanished-over-the-pacific-in-1937-a-theory-suggests-she-survived-a-crash-landing-on-a-remote-island-before-giant-coconut-crabs-consumed-her-remains/articleshow/134964353.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/amelia-earhart-vanished-over-the-pacific-in-1937-a-theory-suggests-she-survived-a-crash-landing-on-a-remote-island-before-giant-coconut-crabs-consumed-her-remains/articleshow/134964353.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T15:55:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134964648,imgsize-694150.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Planned terrorist acts on behalf of Ukraine': Swedish national arrested in Russia]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134964299.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Russia’s FSB has detained a Swedish national accused of planning terrorist acts and sabotage for Ukraine. The agency claims he illegally crossed the border to execute these attacks on military facilities. Identified as Freddy Lindholm, he allegedly trained in drone operations after signing a contract with Ukraine’s army. His detention highlights Russian measures against foreign espionage amid ongoing tensions. The situation remains sensitive with varying international responses to the allegations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/planned-terrorist-acts-on-behalf-of-ukraine-russia-arrests-swedish-man-charges-him-with-illegal-border-crossing/articleshow/134964299.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/planned-terrorist-acts-on-behalf-of-ukraine-russia-arrests-swedish-man-charges-him-with-illegal-border-crossing/articleshow/134964299.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-15T15:52:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134964631,imgsize-25840.cms"/></item></channel></rss>